This project has been the most fun I've had while coding. 
Sure, I've had my frustrations, but I've been able to optimize my code over and over again, find errors I could fix, and improve areas I never would have looked at a few months ago. 
In my two previous projects, retro-mindsweeper and "multi-asset-portfolio-risk-dashboard", 
I never used folders and organized my code in such a manner as in this project. This experience has meant so much to me that I've written an entire research
paper on my discoveries using my code model. 
